# The repository's .gitignore is whitelist-based, so a working checkout carries
# plenty that git never sees — a real .env, compiled binaries, dist/, the history
# JSONL. The Dockerfile already copies path by path; this keeps the build context
# small and makes a stray secret impossible even if that ever changes.
#
# `**` rather than `*`: Docker matches patterns against whole paths and `*` stops
# at a slash, so `*` alone would leave everything below the first level in the
# context. Each re-inclusion needs `/**` for the same reason.
**

!go.mod
!go.sum
!main.go
!bot/**
!budget/**
!config/**
!history/**
!i18n/**
!mode/**
!provider/**
!docker/**

# Test files play no part in the image.
**/*_test.go
